Subject: [PATCH] package/libvirt: mount cgroup v2 without systemd, as docker-engine

Without systemd, libvirt selects cgroupfs-mount (the cgroup v1 hierarchies),
while docker-engine selects cgroupfs-v2-mount and depends on
!BR2_PACKAGE_CGROUPFS_MOUNT: a rootfs with both libvirt and Docker cannot be
configured, and Kconfig drops docker-engine. libvirt supports cgroup v2 since
5.0 (this Buildroot has 7.10), so select cgroupfs-v2-mount instead.

Upstream: not sent (Buildroot master, 2026-11, still selects cgroupfs-mount).
---
diff --git a/package/libvirt/Config.in b/package/libvirt/Config.in
index 0f73128d..a00c4569 100644
--- a/package/libvirt/Config.in
+++ b/package/libvirt/Config.in
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ config BR2_PACKAGE_LIBVIRT
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBXML2
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_ZLIB
 	# run-time dependencies
-	select BR2_PACKAGE_CGROUPFS_MOUNT if !BR2_INIT_SYSTEMD
+	select BR2_PACKAGE_CGROUPFS_V2_MOUNT if !BR2_INIT_SYSTEMD
 	help
 	  Libvirt is collection of software that provides a convenient
 	  way to manage virtual machines and other virtualization
